Let's share the table.

00:31:16.355 --> 00:31:17.757
Share with her?

00:31:17.757 --> 00:31:18.925
Can't she leave?

00:31:18.925 --> 00:31:21.661
I said you sell amazing fried chicken
and brought my friends here.

00:31:21.661 --> 00:31:23.029
Just wait a bit.

00:31:25.097 --> 00:31:26.198
It's hot.

00:31:27.333 --> 00:31:28.834
Why is it so hot in here?

00:31:30.169 --> 00:31:32.872
Ma'am, cancel my order.

00:31:33.739 --> 00:31:34.840
Make some room for her.

00:31:34.840 --> 00:31:35.675
I'm sorry, ma'am.

00:31:37.209 --> 00:31:38.544
Thank you.

00:31:38.544 --> 00:31:40.046
- Hurry.
- Let's sit.

00:31:41.948 --> 00:31:44.450
Three fried chickens,
one spicy whelk salad,

00:31:44.450 --> 00:31:45.551
and five beers, please.

00:31:47.587 --> 00:31:48.421
This looks so good.

00:31:48.688 --> 00:31:50.990
- I told you it was good.
- It looks amazing.

00:32:17.617 --> 00:32:18.351
Il Ri.

00:32:29.695 --> 00:32:30.463
Are you okay?

00:32:37.069 --> 00:32:38.037
Did something happen?

00:33:00.793 --> 00:33:03.362
Hey, slow down.

00:33:04.096 --> 00:33:06.232
Are you possessed or something?
Why are you eating so fast?

00:33:12.972 --> 00:33:14.307
I feel much better.

00:33:22.515 --> 00:33:23.983
No.

00:33:24.884 --> 00:33:26.218
I'm sorry, dude.

00:33:26.619 --> 00:33:28.287
Why am I so clumsy?

00:33:28.287 --> 00:33:31.791
I knew that would happen.
That's why I gave you my jacket.

00:33:32.291 --> 00:33:34.293
Ever since you were in school,

00:33:34.293 --> 00:33:36.762
you were always wearing
whatever you ate on your clothes.

00:33:36.762 --> 00:33:38.898
Tteokbokki, spicy seafood noodle soup,
and so on.

00:33:39.198 --> 00:33:40.099
Stop.

00:33:42.969 --> 00:33:45.338
Now talk to me.

00:33:46.806 --> 00:33:47.807
What's going on?

00:33:48.474 --> 00:33:50.176
What happened?

00:33:50.176 --> 00:33:52.011
Why were you crying like a kid
out in the streets?

00:33:53.212 --> 00:33:54.146
Well,

00:33:55.815 --> 00:33:57.483
I fought with Na Jeong.

00:33:58.751 --> 00:34:00.886
What? And here I thought
it was something big.

00:34:02.121 --> 00:34:04.423
You guys are old enough now,
and you're still fighting?

00:34:04.690 --> 00:34:06.325
Whatever. You don't know what happened.

00:34:15.001 --> 00:34:16.736
Look at you.

00:34:20.406 --> 00:34:21.607
Look at the way he's eating.

00:34:22.575 --> 00:34:23.542
He eats way too much.

00:34:24.944 --> 00:34:26.612
Isn't Jae Hyeon hilarious?

00:34:26.612 --> 00:34:27.747
Totally.

00:34:28.147 --> 00:34:31.651
How does he make it look so delicious
when he eats?

00:34:31.651 --> 00:34:33.686
He's going to be huge, I'm telling you.

00:34:33.686 --> 00:34:36.622
He's already quite taller
than other kids his age.

00:34:36.622 --> 00:34:38.257
And Joo Hyeon sees that...

00:34:38.257 --> 00:34:41.594
and keeps eating like crazy,
saying she has to grow as tall as him.

00:34:42.261 --> 00:34:44.730
I really have to make a lot of money.

00:34:44.730 --> 00:34:46.332
Work hard and feed them well.

00:34:46.332 --> 00:34:48.134
That's the greatest joy...

00:34:48.968 --> 00:34:51.637
and the best investment there is.

00:34:54.040 --> 00:34:54.907
Joo Young.

00:34:55.441 --> 00:34:56.909
Do you even look at my Instagram?

00:34:58.611 --> 00:34:59.612
What are you talking about?

00:35:00.880 --> 00:35:04.517
You never leave any comments.

00:35:05.418 --> 00:35:08.054
You post in the group chat every day.
Do I have to leave comments as well?

00:35:08.487 --> 00:35:10.056
They're different.

00:35:11.157 --> 00:35:13.659
Don't you find
your nephew and niece adorable?

00:35:14.994 --> 00:35:16.329
What are you trying to say?

00:35:17.363 --> 00:35:20.733
They say you have to be jealous of kids...

00:35:20.733 --> 00:35:23.536
for you to have one of your own.

00:35:23.536 --> 00:35:26.606
Then you'll try harder, right?
Be more proactive.

00:35:26.606 --> 00:35:27.707
That's enough.

00:35:28.341 --> 00:35:29.976
She must be frustrated already.

00:35:33.279 --> 00:35:34.447
So...

00:35:34.447 --> 00:35:36.782
what exactly is the problem, Joo Young?

00:35:37.950 --> 00:35:39.719
Is it that Sang Min can't perform?

00:35:40.386 --> 00:35:41.887
Or are you the problem?

00:35:43.322 --> 00:35:44.924
I'll head out first. You finish eating.

00:35:44.924 --> 00:35:46.158
Mom, I'm leaving.

00:35:47.760 --> 00:35:49.161
Thanks for the meal.

00:35:53.199 --> 00:35:54.200
How much is it?

00:35:54.200 --> 00:35:55.534
It's 170 dollars.

00:35:58.304 --> 00:35:59.272
Just a moment.

00:36:03.342 --> 00:36:06.746
I'm telling you,
that means the problem is her husband.

00:36:06.746 --> 00:36:07.613
Why?

00:36:08.014 --> 00:36:11.083
Otherwise, why would Joo Young
always be so on edge?

00:36:12.285 --> 00:36:14.553
They say there are tons of guys in IT...

00:36:14.887 --> 00:36:18.324
with problems down there.

00:36:19.425 --> 00:36:22.295
She can't satisfy her desire
nor have kids.

00:36:22.561 --> 00:36:25.131
How frustrating must that be?

00:36:25.131 --> 00:36:27.800
See, what did I say?

00:36:28.200 --> 00:36:30.603
I told you the problem wasn't Joo Young.
It was her husband.

00:36:30.903 --> 00:36:32.872
This is exactly why I said...

00:36:32.872 --> 00:36:36.208
I had a bad feeling
about guys who collect toys.

00:36:36.208 --> 00:36:37.543
Exactly.

00:36:37.543 --> 00:36:40.680
I didn't like him
from the moment I saw him, either.

00:36:44.150 --> 00:36:45.084
What did you just say?

00:36:45.952 --> 00:36:47.053
Say that again.

00:36:47.720 --> 00:36:49.822
Why are you calling
a perfectly healthy man impotent?

00:36:49.822 --> 00:36:51.591
Joo Young, that's not what I meant.

00:36:51.591 --> 00:36:52.558
Our marriage...

00:36:53.125 --> 00:36:54.727
has no problems.

00:36:54.727 --> 00:36:57.063
Sang Min is so nice to me.

00:36:57.063 --> 00:36:58.931
And I have zero complaints.

00:36:59.599 --> 00:37:02.501
Just because we're having a baby later,
do you think you can make up crap?

00:37:02.902 --> 00:37:04.236
Are we that easy to you?

00:37:04.236 --> 00:37:07.039
Why are you getting so touchy?

00:37:07.039 --> 00:37:08.808
It's not even that big a deal.

00:37:14.180 --> 00:37:16.048
He really is impotent.

00:37:16.048 --> 00:37:16.983
Shut up.

00:37:47.713 --> 00:37:49.515
Open the door. It's me.

00:37:53.219 --> 00:37:55.454
I know you're in there. Open up!

00:38:20.846 --> 00:38:22.048
Why aren't you coming home?

00:38:25.084 --> 00:38:26.819
Are you just going to keep living here?

00:38:26.819 --> 00:38:27.820
With them?

00:38:31.557 --> 00:38:32.391
Fine.

00:38:33.659 --> 00:38:35.695
I didn't come here to fight, so I'll stop.

00:38:38.264 --> 00:38:39.231
Rebecca.

00:38:40.866 --> 00:38:42.268
I'm sorry I broke her arm.

00:38:43.069 --> 00:38:45.304
But think about it from my side.

00:38:45.638 --> 00:38:47.907
It's not even a little figure,
but a huge mannequin.

00:38:48.541 --> 00:38:50.142
It was just too creepy.

00:38:50.142 --> 00:38:52.111
And if something's bothering you,
you can talk to me.

00:38:52.111 --> 00:38:53.546
Why are you talking to a doll?

00:38:53.846 --> 00:38:56.349
Why are you being like this?

00:38:56.816 --> 00:38:58.718
Say something!

00:39:04.123 --> 00:39:06.292
Okay, fine.

00:39:07.526 --> 00:39:10.896
But the reason I came here is to say this.

00:39:12.331 --> 00:39:14.667
We should go to the hospital.

00:39:15.668 --> 00:39:16.902
From what I can see,

00:39:16.902 --> 00:39:19.305
I think you're hurt inside.

00:39:20.006 --> 00:39:22.174
These days, if you get checked out
and get treatment,

00:39:22.174 --> 00:39:23.643
they say most things can be fixed.

00:39:23.643 --> 00:39:25.745
So let's go together, okay?

00:39:32.385 --> 00:39:33.386
Why?

00:39:35.688 --> 00:39:37.790
Does it feel like I'm treating you
like you're crazy?

00:39:37.790 --> 00:39:38.758
Does that upset you?

00:39:40.126 --> 00:39:41.727
It's not that.

00:39:42.495 --> 00:39:45.398
I'm doing this
because I want to help you any way I can.

00:39:59.912 --> 00:40:01.747
I'm so sorry to tell you this,

00:40:02.949 --> 00:40:03.916
but...

00:40:06.085 --> 00:40:08.220
don't ask me anything,
and just divorce me.

00:40:09.522 --> 00:40:10.456
What?

00:40:14.126 --> 00:40:15.361
What's wrong with you?

00:40:16.562 --> 00:40:17.797
I'm saying I'll forgive you.

00:40:17.797 --> 00:40:19.832
What right do you have
to be the one bringing up divorce?

00:40:22.568 --> 00:40:23.469
You're right.

00:40:24.070 --> 00:40:25.304
I know I don't have the right.

00:40:25.605 --> 00:40:28.708
Like you said,
I'm not even in my right mind.

00:40:29.875 --> 00:40:31.811
But living with you...

00:40:34.714 --> 00:40:35.982
felt suffocating.

00:40:37.049 --> 00:40:39.185
All you cared about was pregnancy.

00:40:39.185 --> 00:40:40.453
What am I,
some kind of baby-making machine?

00:40:41.287 --> 00:40:42.154
Am I?

00:40:43.522 --> 00:40:44.624
I really...

00:40:46.659 --> 00:40:48.160
It really felt
like I was going to lose my mind.

00:41:31.671 --> 00:41:33.039
(You have a new notification.)

00:41:33.039 --> 00:41:35.641
(Ovulation day,
High chance of pregnancy)

00:42:14.046 --> 00:42:17.550
My time has passed now.

00:42:18.417 --> 00:42:20.219
It's completely over.

00:42:21.120 --> 00:42:23.556
All that's left for me now...

00:42:24.423 --> 00:42:26.292
is to become a lonely old person...

00:42:26.792 --> 00:42:29.362
and die alone in an empty home.

00:42:29.362 --> 00:42:32.932
You've got your whole future ahead of you.
Why do you say such depressing things?

00:42:32.932 --> 00:42:33.866
Dude.

00:42:35.534 --> 00:42:37.303
When I die,

00:42:38.504 --> 00:42:40.806
since you live right across from me,

00:42:42.341 --> 00:42:44.510
before I rot away completely,

00:42:45.478 --> 00:42:46.979
before I'm completely gone,

00:42:47.847 --> 00:42:50.449
will you bury me somewhere sunny?

00:42:51.417 --> 00:42:52.551
I knew this would happen.

00:42:54.520 --> 00:42:56.489
I knew you'd cause trouble.
Wait right here, okay?

00:43:05.097 --> 00:43:05.932
What?

00:43:07.400 --> 00:43:08.801
Did you just laugh at me?

00:43:10.503 --> 00:43:11.404
Why?

00:43:12.104 --> 00:43:13.105
Do I look funny to you?

00:43:14.407 --> 00:43:16.442
What exactly is so funny?

00:43:18.311 --> 00:43:20.646
- I'm sorry, she's just a bit...
- Hold on a second.

00:43:20.646 --> 00:43:22.148
I definitely heard you.

00:43:22.982 --> 00:43:24.917
You said, "That woman is hilarious."

00:43:24.917 --> 00:43:26.018
That's enough.

00:43:26.018 --> 00:43:28.955
Why did you call me hilarious?

00:43:28.955 --> 00:43:29.956
All right.

00:43:29.956 --> 00:43:32.091
I'm sorry. She's not well.

00:43:32.258 --> 00:43:33.726
Let's go, Lee Il Ri.
Let's go home.

00:43:33.726 --> 00:43:36.028
Hey, where do you think you're going?

00:43:36.028 --> 00:43:37.229
Where do you think you're going?

00:43:37.229 --> 00:43:39.231
I'm a fighter, you know.

00:43:39.231 --> 00:43:40.700
- She's really not well.
- Hey.

00:43:41.701 --> 00:43:42.702
Hey!

00:43:45.638 --> 00:43:47.006
Young lady.

00:43:47.006 --> 00:43:49.208
Just tell me the door code, will you?

00:43:49.208 --> 00:43:51.611
Nope, I don't want to.
I'm not telling you.

00:43:51.611 --> 00:43:54.847
What if I tell you, and you just walk in
whenever you feel like it?

00:43:54.847 --> 00:43:56.449
Then I'll just drag you over
to my place instead.

00:43:56.449 --> 00:43:58.818
No way.

00:43:59.085 --> 00:44:01.787
You've got ulterior motives
with me, don't you?

00:44:01.787 --> 00:44:03.489
Since when?

00:44:03.489 --> 00:44:04.957
You animal.

00:44:08.461 --> 00:44:11.130
But what cologne do you use?

00:44:12.198 --> 00:44:13.466
Why are you like this again?

00:44:14.834 --> 00:44:15.935
It smells nice.

00:44:15.935 --> 00:44:18.004
Right, even back then,

00:44:18.004 --> 00:44:20.373
I always made you give me piggybacks
because I liked this scent.

00:44:21.173 --> 00:44:22.575
I remember.

00:44:23.442 --> 00:44:24.610
How nice.

00:44:25.278 --> 00:44:26.712
Hey, please.

00:44:26.712 --> 00:44:29.248
Just punch in the code!

00:44:29.815 --> 00:44:31.651
Hey, where are we?

00:44:32.518 --> 00:44:34.587
Where did you bring me?

00:44:34.587 --> 00:44:36.155
We're home now.

00:44:44.463 --> 00:44:45.731
Finally.

00:44:46.399 --> 00:44:48.034
You're heavier than when you were a kid.

00:44:51.003 --> 00:44:53.706
Hey, are you taking my shoes off?

00:44:54.373 --> 00:44:56.309
These are designers, you know.

00:44:56.309 --> 00:44:57.209
Wait.

00:44:58.144 --> 00:44:59.979
These are really expensive.

00:44:59.979 --> 00:45:00.680
Got it.

00:45:01.213 --> 00:45:03.049
- Don't steal them.
- I won't.

00:45:08.955 --> 00:45:09.789
Hang on.

00:45:10.489 --> 00:45:11.390
Let's move up.

00:45:22.168 --> 00:45:24.337
You really haven't changed at all.

00:45:25.805 --> 00:45:27.340
Hey, Byeon Sang Gyu.

00:45:27.907 --> 00:45:29.308
You like me, don't you?

00:45:31.644 --> 00:45:32.578
What are you saying?

00:45:33.145 --> 00:45:34.947
You're really drunk right now.

00:45:34.947 --> 00:45:36.616
Let's talk tomorrow
when you're sober, okay?

00:45:36.616 --> 00:45:38.684
Let me say this one more time.

00:45:39.352 --> 00:45:40.886
I don't like you.

00:45:41.654 --> 00:45:44.657
But I feel really lonely today.

00:45:45.658 --> 00:45:46.492
Wait.

00:46:05.745 --> 00:46:07.413
You don't have to like me right now.

00:46:08.948 --> 00:46:10.182
Because I'm going to make you fall for me.

00:46:30.503 --> 00:46:33.105
(Sweet Home Shopping)

00:46:34.573 --> 00:46:36.042
Good morning.

00:46:36.475 --> 00:46:38.210
- What do I do?
- It's okay.

00:46:38.210 --> 00:46:40.713
It's okay. These things happen.

00:46:41.747 --> 00:46:42.915
Don't cry.

00:46:43.749 --> 00:46:45.117
Don't cry over something like this.

00:46:45.618 --> 00:46:46.819
What happened?

00:46:47.520 --> 00:46:48.621
Ask her yourself.

00:46:48.621 --> 00:46:49.488
Let's go.

00:46:56.796 --> 00:46:58.197
Did something happen?

00:46:59.665 --> 00:47:01.834
The producer told her
to leave right away...

00:47:01.834 --> 00:47:03.035
for ruining the broadcast.

00:47:03.402 --> 00:47:04.337
What?

00:47:04.637 --> 00:47:06.739
This is all because of you.

00:47:06.739 --> 00:47:09.308
If you hadn't told those stupid lies,
we wouldn't have gotten on the bad side,

00:47:09.308 --> 00:47:11.844
and we wouldn't have been thrown on air
so suddenly like this.

00:47:11.844 --> 00:47:13.613
How is that my fault?

00:47:14.447 --> 00:47:15.615
And...

00:47:15.615 --> 00:47:18.284
you're the ones
who wanted to be on air more.

00:47:18.284 --> 00:47:21.220
It's not like I wanted to go in
this unprepared.

00:47:22.488 --> 00:47:24.056
Ms. Cho, it's your fault.

00:47:24.357 --> 00:47:26.993
Because of you,
everyone at the company hates us now.

00:47:28.227 --> 00:47:30.429
What are we supposed to do?

00:47:35.268 --> 00:47:37.236
What am I supposed to do?

00:47:38.738 --> 00:47:39.438
It's okay.

00:47:39.438 --> 00:47:42.208
(Sanmaeul Fermented Soybean Stew)

00:47:48.447 --> 00:47:51.083
(Sanmaeul Fermented Soybean Stew)

00:48:04.130 --> 00:48:06.332
You're all ready, right?

00:48:07.300 --> 00:48:09.435
Since it's Ms. Yang's first broadcast,

00:48:09.435 --> 00:48:10.770
don't try to do too much.

00:48:10.770 --> 00:48:12.939
And don't miss a single word
of my instructions.

00:48:12.939 --> 00:48:14.640
Even if you hear something in your in-ear,

00:48:14.640 --> 00:48:16.309
don't lose your focus.

00:48:16.309 --> 00:48:17.310
Okay.

00:48:17.310 --> 00:48:19.378
All right, let's go.

00:48:21.247 --> 00:48:22.715
We're live in five seconds.

00:48:27.053 --> 00:48:29.855
Three, two, one.

00:48:31.057 --> 00:48:31.958
Welcome.

00:48:31.958 --> 00:48:34.060
This is delicious
Sanmaeul Fermented Soybean Stew.

00:48:34.060 --> 00:48:35.461
I'm Hong Seon Young.

00:48:35.461 --> 00:48:37.897
And I'm show host Yang Mi Sook.

00:48:37.897 --> 00:48:40.833
Lately, with the trend
toward healthy foods,

00:48:40.833 --> 00:48:43.936
what food is getting the most attention?

00:48:43.936 --> 00:48:46.305
Fermented soybean stew.

00:48:46.305 --> 00:48:47.873
As a dish with high protein
and low calories,

00:48:47.873 --> 00:48:50.343
it's popular with everyone,
men and women, young and old.

00:48:50.343 --> 00:48:52.878
And as a fermented food,
it's incredibly good for your health.

00:48:52.878 --> 00:48:54.680
Since it's hard to make at home,

00:48:54.680 --> 00:48:57.049
if you stock up in your fridge now,

00:48:57.049 --> 00:48:58.651
you'll feel completely set.

00:48:58.651 --> 00:48:59.852
Yes, so...

00:48:59.852 --> 00:49:01.387
And if you look here,

00:49:01.387 --> 00:49:04.790
we've specially prepared
Sanmaeul Fermented Soybean Stew today.

00:49:04.790 --> 00:49:07.693
You all know you could only get this
in stores until now, right?

00:49:07.693 --> 00:49:10.329
Ms. Yang, you're talking way too fast.

00:49:10.963 --> 00:49:12.331
And you're talking way more
than the main host.

00:49:12.999 --> 00:49:14.834
Let's look here.

00:49:14.834 --> 00:49:17.336
The most important thing
about fermented soybean stew...

00:49:17.336 --> 00:49:18.671
is the ingredient.

00:49:18.904 --> 00:49:21.040
Now, what kind of soybean is this?

00:49:21.040 --> 00:49:23.709
It's said to have been served
on the king's royal table long ago.

00:49:23.709 --> 00:49:26.078
The famous Jangdan soybean from Paju.

00:49:26.078 --> 00:49:30.149
It's 100 percent domestically grown,
pure soybean.

00:49:30.149 --> 00:49:31.317
Ms. Yang, can't you hear me?

00:49:32.218 --> 00:49:34.120
Why are you acting out
when you're the co-host?

00:49:34.654 --> 00:49:35.521
I'm sorry.

00:49:41.160 --> 00:49:42.828
And we take those Jangdan soybeans...

00:49:42.828 --> 00:49:46.465
and boil them in a cauldron like this
for about two hours,

00:49:46.465 --> 00:49:49.402
then let them steam
for about three and a half hours.

00:49:49.402 --> 00:49:52.038
And then ferment them on a warm floor,

00:49:55.608 --> 00:49:56.542
and look at this.

00:49:56.542 --> 00:49:58.844
Do you see these pale white strands?

00:50:01.314 --> 00:50:02.181
Okay.

00:50:03.883 --> 00:50:05.251
Shall we try some?

00:50:05.251 --> 00:50:08.120
It looks so delicious. I'll try some too.

00:50:09.155 --> 00:50:10.089
Yes.

00:50:17.663 --> 00:50:18.798
Don't spit it out.

00:50:18.798 --> 00:50:21.033
Swallow it!

00:50:21.033 --> 00:50:21.767
Please.

00:50:33.079 --> 00:50:34.380
Do you think broadcasting is a joke?

00:50:35.248 --> 00:50:37.183
The comment section
is blowing up right now.

00:50:37.717 --> 00:50:39.752
They're saying this is like a comedy,
not a home shopping show.

00:50:40.253 --> 00:50:43.656
They're saying they've never seen
someone spit food out like that,

00:50:43.656 --> 00:50:45.591
and that it was so disgusting!

00:50:47.159 --> 00:50:50.363
And why did you do the show by yourself?

00:50:50.630 --> 00:50:53.165
Did you forget that I'm the main host,
and you're the co-host?

00:50:53.699 --> 00:50:55.868
We're supposed to work together,

00:50:55.868 --> 00:50:57.536
but you're just desperate to stand out!

00:50:58.104 --> 00:51:01.107
Do you have any idea how uncomfortable
that makes the viewers?

00:51:02.108 --> 00:51:03.175
How are you going...

00:51:03.442 --> 00:51:06.178
to take responsibility for this outcome?

00:51:39.078 --> 00:51:40.980
Hello.

00:51:42.114 --> 00:51:43.449
Hello.

00:51:43.449 --> 00:51:45.518
- You're here for the kids today.
- Yes.

00:51:45.518 --> 00:51:46.852
- Just a moment.
- Okay.

00:52:01.233 --> 00:52:02.101
Mom.

00:52:02.101 --> 00:52:03.269
- Mom.
- Hey.

00:52:04.070 --> 00:52:07.173
Mom, can we go play
on the playground first?

00:52:07.173 --> 00:52:07.907
Sure.

00:52:11.010 --> 00:52:12.211
- Thank you.
- Sure.

00:52:15.781 --> 00:52:16.949
Hello.

00:52:17.350 --> 00:52:19.952
Whose father are you, if I may ask?

00:52:19.952 --> 00:52:21.787
I'm Joo Ri Ae's dad.

00:52:21.787 --> 00:52:23.256
My wife had to work, so I came.

00:52:24.357 --> 00:52:26.125
Just a moment.

00:52:31.230 --> 00:52:32.465
You're kind of cute.

00:52:32.832 --> 00:52:34.767
My wife is in a meeting.

00:52:34.767 --> 00:52:36.369
She told me not to call her.

00:52:37.169 --> 00:52:38.738
But still...

00:52:39.772 --> 00:52:40.940
You don't believe me?

00:52:41.474 --> 00:52:44.243
She's in an important meeting right now
and told me not to call at all.

00:52:46.479 --> 00:52:48.514
But under kindergarten rules,

00:52:48.514 --> 00:52:51.317
we can't let a child go
without the mother's consent.

00:52:53.586 --> 00:52:56.822
Look, her mom had work to do.

00:52:56.822 --> 00:52:58.224
That's why she sent me.

00:52:59.025 --> 00:53:00.760
If you're really that worried,

00:53:01.160 --> 00:53:03.229
bring Ri Ae out and let her see me.

00:53:03.229 --> 00:53:05.631
If she says she doesn't want to go,
I'll just leave.

00:53:06.832 --> 00:53:07.967
Just a moment.

00:53:14.607 --> 00:53:16.776
But Ri Ae says
she doesn't want to go to China.

00:53:16.776 --> 00:53:17.944
She says her stepmom is scary.

00:53:25.017 --> 00:53:26.285
The power is currently off...

00:53:29.789 --> 00:53:30.690
Dad?

00:53:32.091 --> 00:53:34.193
My sweet girl.

00:53:37.997 --> 00:53:39.498
Didn't you miss me?

00:53:39.498 --> 00:53:41.067
I missed you.

00:53:42.001 --> 00:53:43.102
Do you believe me now?

00:53:44.637 --> 00:53:46.138
I told you, I'm Ri Ae's dad.

00:53:47.540 --> 00:53:48.407
Let's go!

00:53:51.677 --> 00:53:55.147
You're the delivery guy from Hanmae-dong,
Joo Cheol Geun, right?

00:53:55.781 --> 00:53:57.350
Nice to see you.

00:53:58.384 --> 00:53:59.218
Who are you?

00:53:59.218 --> 00:54:01.887
Me? I'm Cho Na Jeong
from Hanmae Middle School.

00:54:02.888 --> 00:54:04.757
Sorry, I don't remember.

00:54:04.757 --> 00:54:06.726
How can you not remember?

00:54:06.726 --> 00:54:08.594
You asked me to go to karaoke with you,

00:54:08.594 --> 00:54:11.631
and Mi Sook got mad
and grabbed my hair and we fought.

00:54:13.132 --> 00:54:14.800
I'm telling you, I don't know you.

00:54:14.800 --> 00:54:16.936
Anyway, how have you been all this time?

00:54:16.936 --> 00:54:18.004
Have you been well?

00:54:18.237 --> 00:54:20.539
But does Ri Ae's mom even know...

00:54:20.539 --> 00:54:22.508
you're taking her?

00:54:23.175 --> 00:54:24.877
Sir, I'm sorry,

00:54:24.877 --> 00:54:26.479
but you should talk to the mother first,

00:54:26.479 --> 00:54:28.214
and then take her.

00:54:29.548 --> 00:54:32.285
What kind of nonsense is this?
Get out of my way.

00:54:34.453 --> 00:54:35.922
Moms, perfect timing.

00:54:35.922 --> 00:54:38.658
He's trying to kidnap a child.
Please hold on to him.

00:54:38.658 --> 00:54:39.592
Police!

00:54:40.226 --> 00:54:41.727
- Let go.
- Call the police.

00:54:43.329 --> 00:54:44.263
Hold him tight.

00:54:44.263 --> 00:54:45.765
That's it, hold him tight.

00:54:46.933 --> 00:54:48.267
Back off, you crazy woman.

00:54:53.306 --> 00:54:55.308
What do you think you're doing right now?

00:54:55.708 --> 00:54:57.843
Why are you dragging in
someone who's done nothing wrong?

00:54:57.843 --> 00:54:59.845
I'm the kid's father,
and I want to take her with me.

00:54:59.845 --> 00:55:01.314
What's wrong with that?

00:55:01.314 --> 00:55:04.250
There's nothing wrong
with a dad taking his kid.

00:55:04.250 --> 00:55:05.818
But you live overseas now, don't you?

00:55:05.818 --> 00:55:07.620
If you take her
without even telling her mom,

00:55:07.620 --> 00:55:09.889
that's a problem.

00:55:11.691 --> 00:55:14.260
And where did this random nobody
crawl out from?

00:55:14.260 --> 00:55:15.428
Will you shut up?

00:55:16.062 --> 00:55:17.196
Who are you calling a nobody?

00:55:17.496 --> 00:55:19.899
Calm down.

00:55:19.899 --> 00:55:20.666
Please sit down.

00:55:21.834 --> 00:55:22.635
Mi Sook.

00:55:25.171 --> 00:55:27.340
You bastard, who are you to take my kid?

00:55:27.340 --> 00:55:28.774
Who do you think you are?

00:55:28.774 --> 00:55:30.409
I told you to leave my daughter alone.

00:55:30.409 --> 00:55:32.378
I told you to leave my daughter alone!

00:55:32.378 --> 00:55:34.113
Are you crazy?

00:55:34.680 --> 00:55:36.482
Is Ri Ae only your daughter?

00:55:36.482 --> 00:55:37.984
She's my daughter too.

00:55:39.652 --> 00:55:41.954
A guy who lets his kid
watch him beat her mom every day?

00:55:41.954 --> 00:55:43.656
What kind of father does that?

00:55:43.656 --> 00:55:47.059
A guy who doesn't pay a single penny
in living expenses? How is that a father?

00:55:47.693 --> 00:55:51.664
Where did you stash my hard-earned money?

00:55:51.664 --> 00:55:53.065
Bring me my money!

00:55:53.065 --> 00:55:55.101
Give me my money, you bastard.

00:55:55.101 --> 00:55:56.269
Give me my money.

00:55:56.269 --> 00:55:57.270
Damn it.

00:55:59.005 --> 00:56:00.640
- Mi Sook.
- Damn it.

00:56:01.040 --> 00:56:01.941
Are you okay?

00:56:03.809 --> 00:56:04.944
Let go of me.

00:56:05.645 --> 00:56:06.679
You!

00:56:20.626 --> 00:56:21.494
Here.

00:56:24.931 --> 00:56:26.098
Right, where's Ri Ae?

00:56:26.565 --> 00:56:28.367
She's fine with our nanny.

00:56:28.367 --> 00:56:29.402
Don't worry.

00:56:30.336 --> 00:56:31.203
Thanks.

00:56:39.211 --> 00:56:42.148
He's Joo Cheol Geun from back then, right?

00:56:46.586 --> 00:56:47.453
Yeah, that's him.

00:56:48.287 --> 00:56:50.056
This is so humiliating.

00:56:50.056 --> 00:56:51.857
Picking trash like that
and calling him my husband.

00:56:51.857 --> 00:56:54.193
I really must have been blind.

00:56:55.294 --> 00:56:56.696
Why?

00:56:56.696 --> 00:56:58.230
You got married, ran a business together,

00:56:58.230 --> 00:56:59.732
and made a lot of money.

00:57:00.199 --> 00:57:01.601
There's nothing to be ashamed of.

00:57:02.301 --> 00:57:03.536
A lot of money?

00:57:05.705 --> 00:57:08.808
Hey, I earned all of that
doing live commerce.

00:57:08.808 --> 00:57:10.576
That jerk didn't do a thing.

00:57:10.576 --> 00:57:12.812
But you know what's really unbelievable?

00:57:14.146 --> 00:57:17.316
That piece of trash
went crazy over some woman...

00:57:17.316 --> 00:57:19.986
and siphoned off every last bit
of the money I earned and all our assets.

00:57:21.520 --> 00:57:23.022
And you know what's even more absurd?

00:57:23.322 --> 00:57:24.957
No matter how awful he is,

00:57:25.524 --> 00:57:27.460
if I don't have a proper job,

00:57:27.960 --> 00:57:29.428
they say they'll send her to her dad.

00:57:29.428 --> 00:57:31.297
They say there's nothing they can do.

00:57:32.365 --> 00:57:34.867
That's why I was so desperate
to get into Sweet Home Shopping.

00:57:37.436 --> 00:57:40.806
But what am I supposed to do now?

00:57:40.806 --> 00:57:44.076
At this rate,
it's obvious I'm going to get fired.

00:57:45.978 --> 00:57:47.013
Damn it.

00:57:49.916 --> 00:57:50.950
If...

00:57:51.918 --> 00:57:53.819
they really take Ri Ae away from me,

00:57:54.720 --> 00:57:56.856
how am I supposed to live on, Na Jeong?

00:57:57.823 --> 00:57:59.959
How am I supposed to go on?

00:58:02.595 --> 00:58:04.597
Damn it.

00:58:15.174 --> 00:58:18.444
Last time, because Ms. Cho showed up,

00:58:18.444 --> 00:58:20.079
I couldn't properly apologize.

00:58:21.914 --> 00:58:22.915
I'm sorry.

00:58:26.152 --> 00:58:29.155
But when I even got rejected
from Samjin Shopping as my last shot,

00:58:29.722 --> 00:58:30.690
it just felt so unfair.

00:58:32.224 --> 00:58:35.428
Still, I'm not going to stop here.

00:58:36.262 --> 00:58:38.230
I'll fight it all the way to the end.

00:58:38.898 --> 00:58:40.533
It took so much for me
to become a show host.

00:58:40.833 --> 00:58:43.603
I can't just let myself be branded
like this and get destroyed.

00:58:45.004 --> 00:58:46.105
Right, Producer Noh?

00:58:49.241 --> 00:58:51.510
Seon Min, I'm sorry.

00:58:53.412 --> 00:58:55.681
I don't think I can help you anymore.

00:58:57.817 --> 00:59:00.353
I know full well
how hard things are for you.

00:59:00.987 --> 00:59:02.688
But the pressure from the company
is just too much.

00:59:03.389 --> 00:59:05.891
I was ready to take it if they fired me.

00:59:05.891 --> 00:59:07.526
I thought I could handle that somehow.

00:59:09.095 --> 00:59:11.430
But they said they'd fire my wife too.

00:59:14.634 --> 00:59:16.502
I'm really sorry.

00:59:17.970 --> 00:59:19.205
No, Producer Noh.

00:59:21.007 --> 00:59:22.675
I completely understand.

00:59:22.975 --> 00:59:26.145
Anyone else would've just looked
the other way,

00:59:27.713 --> 00:59:28.814
but you helped me out, Producer Noh.

00:59:29.949 --> 00:59:32.385
I know how much you've helped me
up to now.

00:59:37.556 --> 00:59:40.226
I'm sorry,
I forgot I had another appointment.

00:59:40.760 --> 00:59:42.028
I'll get going first.

00:59:46.399 --> 00:59:47.600
I never got to return this back then.

00:59:49.568 --> 00:59:50.603
I'll see you next time.

01:00:02.248 --> 01:00:05.484
If I don't have a proper job,
they'll send her to her dad.

01:00:05.484 --> 01:00:07.453
They say she doesn't need some "good mom."

01:00:15.895 --> 01:00:17.163
Mom, look at this.

01:00:18.230 --> 01:00:19.298
What's this?

01:00:19.632 --> 01:00:20.866
A present for Ri Ae.

01:00:24.937 --> 01:00:27.206
But Mom, is Ri Ae going to China now?

01:00:28.908 --> 01:00:30.943
No, who said that?

01:00:31.477 --> 01:00:33.412
But Ri Ae's dad came today.

01:00:33.713 --> 01:00:36.249
Do I have to say goodbye to her now?

01:00:39.118 --> 01:00:40.253
No.

01:00:45.391 --> 01:00:47.793
You did an amazing job. It's so pretty.

01:00:56.802 --> 01:00:57.703
Here.

01:00:59.238 --> 01:01:00.072
What's this?

01:01:00.072 --> 01:01:03.743
They are some tips I've thought
were important.

01:01:03.743 --> 01:01:05.978
I've been jotting them down for a while.

01:01:05.978 --> 01:01:07.813
I thought it might help
if you looked through it.

01:01:08.247 --> 01:01:09.115
Take a look.

01:01:10.816 --> 01:01:11.751
Hey, Cho Na Jeong.

01:01:12.251 --> 01:01:13.085
Yeah?

01:01:14.153 --> 01:01:16.155
Why are you doing this for me?

01:01:16.856 --> 01:01:18.691
If I fail,
it only works out better for you.

01:01:19.091 --> 01:01:20.293
So why are you doing this for me?

01:01:21.961 --> 01:01:24.297
Sure, I kind of resent you.

01:01:25.197 --> 01:01:26.132
But...

01:01:26.465 --> 01:01:28.668
I want to protect my son's girlfriend.
That's why.

01:01:29.368 --> 01:01:30.202
Okay?

01:01:34.774 --> 01:01:38.377
Can you just teach me yourself?

01:01:39.078 --> 01:01:39.912
What?

01:01:40.179 --> 01:01:42.848
Don't you remember?
I was terrible at studying.

01:01:43.916 --> 01:01:46.652
And how am I supposed
to go through all this on my own?

01:01:56.696 --> 01:01:57.663
Here.

01:01:57.663 --> 01:02:00.199
If I pass on the tricks I used the most,
here's what I'd say.

01:02:00.199 --> 01:02:01.634
When you're doing a food show,

01:02:01.634 --> 01:02:03.536
because the food
has been simmering forever,

01:02:03.536 --> 01:02:05.271
it's insanely hot.

01:02:05.271 --> 01:02:07.073
First, scoop up one spoonful.

01:02:07.073 --> 01:02:08.841
Then start your lines.

01:02:08.841 --> 01:02:11.477
While you're talking,
it'll naturally cool down.

01:02:11.477 --> 01:02:13.546
At least you won't have to worry
about burning yourself.

01:02:13.546 --> 01:02:15.615
I didn't even know that.

01:02:15.615 --> 01:02:17.717
And when you explain a product,

01:02:17.717 --> 01:02:20.019
you don't need long-winded explanations
or anything.

01:02:20.019 --> 01:02:21.787
Out of everything you feel about it,

01:02:21.787 --> 01:02:23.856
pick the one point
that would tempt you the most,

01:02:23.856 --> 01:02:25.691
and emphasize that. That's the key.

01:02:27.093 --> 01:02:28.861
And for things like cosmetics,

01:02:28.861 --> 01:02:30.630
it's way more natural if you actually
try them yourself first, right?

01:02:30.630 --> 01:02:31.664
Of course.

01:02:31.664 --> 01:02:34.100
You can just mention
stuff like brightening or anti-aging,

01:02:34.100 --> 01:02:36.936
but you only know how it goes on
or how long it lasts by using it.

01:02:36.936 --> 01:02:38.337
Exactly.

01:02:38.337 --> 01:02:39.538
Before a show,

01:02:39.538 --> 01:02:41.841
I use everything myself
for days beforehand.

01:02:41.841 --> 01:02:43.409
I even keep testing notes.

01:02:43.676 --> 01:02:46.746
What matters most is turning everything
into your own words.

01:02:47.647 --> 01:02:49.315
- Testing notes.
- Yeah.

01:02:53.286 --> 01:02:54.086
Here they are.

01:02:54.820 --> 01:02:55.655
This is it.

01:02:55.655 --> 01:02:57.223
- You really wrote the key points.
- Yeah.

01:02:59.926 --> 01:03:01.894
Scoop up a spoonful like this.

01:03:01.894 --> 01:03:02.828
Scoop up a spoonful.

01:03:02.828 --> 01:03:04.597
Then talk while you let it cool.

01:03:05.698 --> 01:03:09.735
Everyone, see the steam rising?
This is when it tastes the best, right?

01:03:10.269 --> 01:03:13.539
Everyone, see the steam rising?
This is when it tastes the best, right?

01:03:13.940 --> 01:03:15.441
I'll try this.

01:03:15.975 --> 01:03:17.643
I'll try this.

01:03:21.781 --> 01:03:22.715
This is it.

01:03:27.286 --> 01:03:28.487
This is it.

01:03:28.487 --> 01:03:30.656
Yeah, there you go.
Let's try again.

01:03:31.457 --> 01:03:33.426
You've all had this happen, right?

01:03:33.426 --> 01:03:35.962
In the morning,
you pack soup in a lunchbox,

01:03:35.962 --> 01:03:37.530
and it leaks all over your bag.

01:03:37.530 --> 01:03:39.732
That's such a disaster.
Even your clothes...

01:03:39.732 --> 01:03:41.601
In parts like that
where you're emphasizing something,

01:03:41.601 --> 01:03:44.670
it's good if we make eye contact
and give each other a little smile.

01:03:44.670 --> 01:03:47.940
If you only stare at the camera,
it feels like you're off on your own.

01:03:47.940 --> 01:03:49.575
Right. Reactions.

01:03:50.009 --> 01:03:53.012
It'd be nice if you could cue
when we should pause and react.

01:03:53.012 --> 01:03:54.246
Okay.

01:03:54.880 --> 01:03:57.350
So the timing of the pauses is important.

01:03:57.350 --> 01:03:58.651
Yeah.

01:04:10.796 --> 01:04:11.631
Good luck.

01:04:15.901 --> 01:04:18.571
Three, two, one.

01:04:19.672 --> 01:04:22.041
Hello, everyone.
I'm show host Hong Seon Young.

01:04:22.041 --> 01:04:23.876
Hello, I'm Yang Mi Sook.

01:04:24.110 --> 01:04:27.747
Everyone, what do you worry about
when you use food containers?

01:04:27.747 --> 01:04:30.683
After just a short time,
they get stained and pick up smells.

01:04:30.683 --> 01:04:33.552
You're nervous
they might be leaching harmful chemicals.

01:04:33.552 --> 01:04:36.722
You wonder if they're okay in the freezer
or safe in the microwave.

01:04:36.722 --> 01:04:38.291
Isn't that right?

01:04:38.291 --> 01:04:41.427
Right. Once you buy them, you want
to use them cleanly for a long time.

01:04:41.427 --> 01:04:43.229
But there's just so much to worry about.

01:04:44.096 --> 01:04:47.099
What brand pops into your head
at times like that?

01:04:47.099 --> 01:04:48.567
Yes, Gotlock.

01:04:48.567 --> 01:04:51.470
It's held the number one spot
in brand power for ten years straight,

01:04:51.470 --> 01:04:53.506
and earned the notoriously strict
LOHAS certification...

01:04:53.506 --> 01:04:55.541
eight years in a row.

01:04:55.541 --> 01:04:59.445
It's the brand moms trust
and reach for first.

01:04:59.445 --> 01:05:02.748
Honestly, every home has
at least one piece of Gotlock, right?

01:05:02.748 --> 01:05:03.583
Exactly.

01:05:03.583 --> 01:05:05.518
This time I switched out
all the containers at home...

01:05:05.518 --> 01:05:07.286
and replaced them with Gotlock.

01:05:07.286 --> 01:05:09.989
Before, no matter how much
I cleaned the fridge,

01:05:09.989 --> 01:05:13.326
it still felt cluttered,
and faint side-dish smells kept lingering.

01:05:13.326 --> 01:05:15.394
Now it's completely spotless.

01:05:15.394 --> 01:05:18.431
Now I really get why homemakers
keep looking for Gotlock.

01:05:18.431 --> 01:05:20.266
- I get it now.
- Right.

01:05:20.266 --> 01:05:23.936
There's a reason
so many homemakers trust and choose it.

01:05:23.936 --> 01:05:26.906
Now, with just about a minute left
in our show,

01:05:26.906 --> 01:05:28.808
our remaining stock is almost...

01:05:29.709 --> 01:05:30.876
Yes, completely sold out!

01:05:30.876 --> 01:05:31.744
We did it.

01:05:33.112 --> 01:05:35.314
Everyone, thank you so much.

01:05:35.314 --> 01:05:38.884
Our smart shoppers
really do know how to decide fast.

01:05:39.852 --> 01:05:43.022
To everyone who joined us today,
thank you from the bottom of our hearts.

01:05:43.022 --> 01:05:44.590
Changing what goes on your family's table.

01:05:44.590 --> 01:05:47.159
It's not too late to start today.

01:05:47.159 --> 01:05:50.062
If you missed today's order,
please look forward to our next show.

01:05:50.062 --> 01:05:52.331
Here's to always staying healthy
and running a thrifty home.

01:05:52.331 --> 01:05:53.833
We'll be cheering you on.

01:05:54.900 --> 01:05:56.869
Thank you so much, everyone.

01:05:59.839 --> 01:06:00.906
Great work, everyone.

01:06:10.483 --> 01:06:11.517
Are you heading home already?

01:06:11.984 --> 01:06:14.086
Hey, you worked hard today.

01:06:15.388 --> 01:06:17.490
Do you have to get home early today
or something?

01:06:17.490 --> 01:06:19.125
No, not really.

01:06:19.425 --> 01:06:22.194
We're grabbing a drink with the others
at Million Hof tonight.

01:06:22.194 --> 01:06:23.296
Do you want to come?

01:06:23.296 --> 01:06:25.097
I'm buying.

01:06:25.798 --> 01:06:26.866
Really?

01:06:27.233 --> 01:06:28.367
If you're buying, I should go.

01:06:29.435 --> 01:06:30.202
Let's go.

01:06:36.042 --> 01:06:38.778
Thanks for everything.

01:06:38.778 --> 01:06:39.845
It's nothing.

01:06:40.980 --> 01:06:42.281
I told you, right?

01:06:42.281 --> 01:06:43.883
I'm getting your help for now.

01:06:43.883 --> 01:06:46.152
But don't think
I'll be cutting you slack forever.

01:06:46.953 --> 01:06:49.355
My school might not be as good as yours,

01:06:49.355 --> 01:06:50.923
but I have more grit than you do.

01:06:50.923 --> 01:06:52.592
Yang Mi Sook.

01:06:52.592 --> 01:06:54.427
You really do have pride.

01:06:55.127 --> 01:06:56.395
Hold on.

01:06:59.432 --> 01:07:00.333
(Nanny)

01:07:11.644 --> 01:07:12.612
I'm sorry.

01:07:12.778 --> 01:07:13.579
It's okay.

01:07:33.766 --> 01:07:35.468
Why isn't she picking up?

01:08:32.692 --> 01:08:34.827
(Don't call me ma'am)

01:08:35.294 --> 01:08:36.862
Why isn't she picking up?

01:08:36.862 --> 01:08:37.797
Min Woo.

01:08:37.797 --> 01:08:38.831
Noh Min Jun.

01:08:40.132 --> 01:08:41.968
We're getting a divorce.

01:08:41.968 --> 01:08:43.436
Tell me why.

01:08:44.737 --> 01:08:46.739
Do I look okay today?

01:08:47.506 --> 01:08:48.341
Gu Joo Young.

01:08:48.341 --> 01:08:51.877
You know how there are guys
who have that uniquely nice smell?

01:08:56.115 --> 01:08:58.517
Am I some nanny
who gets a paycheck from you?

01:08:59.385 --> 01:09:00.786
Is Mom your maid who cleans up after you?

01:09:00.786 --> 01:09:01.754
I should just shut
that smart mouth of yours.

01:09:01.754 --> 01:09:04.457
Go on, do it.
If you think you can, hit me.

01:09:04.457 --> 01:09:06.492
So you're going back?

01:09:07.193 --> 01:09:08.995
Use this chance
to step back from childcare.

01:09:11.931 --> 01:09:13.933
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)